# QA Reporting Rules

After testing is completed:

Create a QA report.

Do not fix any bugs.

---

## Report Location

Store reports inside:

QA-Reports/


Each test run should create a new folder:

Example:

QA-Reports/
  YYYY-MM-DD-test-name/


---

## Required Files

Create:

report.md

bugs.txt


Folder structure:

QA-Reports/
└── checkout-test/
    |
    ├── report.md
    ├── bugs.txt
    └── screenshots/

---

## Bug Report Format

For every issue include:

- Bug ID
- Title
- Severity
- Page URL
- Steps to reproduce
- Expected result
- Actual result
- Screenshot path
- Console errors
- Network errors
- Possible cause

---

## Screenshots

For:

- UI bugs
- Failed steps
- Unexpected behavior

Save screenshots inside:

screenshots/


Example:

screenshots/
  bug-001.png


---

## Videos

For failed flows:

Record video if possible.

---

## Summary

At the end include:

Testing completed:

- Flow name
- Passed steps
- Failed steps

Issues found:

- Critical:
- High:
- Medium:
- Low:

Created files:

- Reports
- Screenshots
- Videos
